{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Swear — He made them swear.</b> He made them swear that they would make their children swear. And why did he not make his sons swear that they would carry him to the land of Canaan immediately, as Jacob made swear? Joseph said: I was a ruler in Egypt and it was in my power to do so, but my sons — Egypt will not let them do it. Therefore he made them swear that when they are redeemed and leave there, they shall carry him." "<b>And you shall carry up my bones from here with you.</b> To his brothers he swore thus — this teaches that they also brought up the bones of all the tribes with them, as it says אִתְּכֶם, 'with you' (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:00.442586345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}